   "en_span":"chapters/factors.qmd:268-268",
   "tr_span":"chapters/factors.fr.qmd:244-244",
   "proposition":"The French text states that the author renamed the r4ds metapackage to r4dses, tidied DESCRIPTION and .Rbuildignore, deleted unneeded files, and obtained zero errors, warnings and notes from devtools::check(). The English section says only that fct_inorder() sets level order to match order of appearance in the data.",
   "reader_consequence":"A French reader in the middle of the fct_inorder() explanation meets a first-person note about packaging an unrelated book repository. It has no bearing on factors, names a package (r4ds/r4dses) the handbook never uses, and leads the reader to think the handbook expects them to run devtools::check() on a book package.",
   "confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"By appearance / Par apparence",
   "segment_index":"S17.P1",
   "kind":"added",
   "en_span":"chapters/factors.qmd:268-268",
   "tr_span":"chapters/factors.fr.qmd:246-246",
   "proposition":"The French text states that the book repository is partly an R package and that devtools::install_github(\"cienciadedatos/r4ds\") installs the book dependencies by reading the DESCRIPTION file it contains. The English has no such statement anywhere in this chapter.",
   "reader_consequence":"A French reader may run devtools::install_github(\"cienciadedatos/r4ds\") believing it installs the dependencies of this handbook. It installs an unrelated Spanish translation of R for Data Science and does not provide forcats, aweek or the handbook datasets.",
   "confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Reduce into \"Other\" / Reduire en \"Autre\"",
   "segment_index":"S23.P1",
   "kind":"code_mismatch",
   "en_span":"chapters/factors.qmd:403-403",
   "tr_span":"chapters/factors.fr.qmd:366-366",
   "proposition":"The French prose names the fct_other() argument as `maintenir = `; the argument is `keep = `, and `keep = ` is what the adjacent code chunk (fr lines 368-376) actually uses.",
   "reader_consequence":"A French reader who follows the prose writes fct_other(hospital, maintenir = c(...)) and gets an unused-argument error, with no clue from the sentence that the real argument name is keep.",
   "confidence":"high"}
